13882	{"artifactId":"LLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1-s11","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-c2ba6fa62a148ed1-s11-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:14:25.200Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers s11's acceptance criteria ac1-ac5 (EXT-…-s11) and ac6 / S011:FR001 (removal of the MCP server's temporary store allowance), each mapped in §5.","evidence":"EXT.md:18-22 lists ac1-ac5 (step tools run in the daemon with the same result; a token survives an MCP restart; named errors when the daemon is unreachable or too old; the MCP import graph opens no store; prompt/schema/state pass through). DEF.md:115 has S011:FR001 'temporary allowance … is removed', and DEF.md:404 records the stakeholder's ac6. LLD §2.2/2.3/2.7, §3.2, and the §5 acceptance table cover all six. [files: docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/EXT.md, docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Dropping MCP sampling (D3) and adding the vector-store owner rule (D4) go beyond the defined criteria.","evidence":"ac4 already requires that nothing in the MCP import graph opens 'the graph store or the vector store'. The getLanceConn owner rule (D4) widens that from the MCP server's code to every process; the LLD flags this itself in §9 as needing an amendment. The sampling removal is a stakeholder decision (D3), and ac5 speaks about step prompts, not the one-shot analyzer's inner calls. No non-goal in DEF.md §3 is built.","action":"Resolve the §9 open question (amend the Story's criteria with D4) before approval so the extra rule is tracked.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the review wait (review-step/phases/start.ts:151) and the code-review wait (code-review-step/handler.ts:689) pass only { timeoutMs }, and ReviewStreamOpts.signal exists but is never filled.","evidence":"start.ts:151: `(deps.reviewByDaemon ?? reviewArtifactStream)({ artifactPath: a.mdPath, repo: a.repo }, { timeoutMs })`. handler.ts:689: `{ timeoutMs: DAEMON_CODE_REVIEW_WAIT_MS }`. daemon-stream.ts:419 declares `readonly signal?: AbortSignal`. [files: src/mcp/review-step/phases/start.ts, src/mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts, src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon's stream server gives each stream an AbortSignal that fires when the socket closes, and it answers an unknown stream method with a plain 'unknown method: …' line.","evidence":"server.ts:215 sends `{ id, error: `unknown method: ${request.method}` }`. server.ts:220-226 aborts the controller on socket 'close'/'error'. server.ts:241 calls `handler(request.params, sendStream, abortController.signal)`. The workflow.review and codeReview.run stream handlers pass that signal into their runs (workflow-review-rpc.ts:104, code-review-rpc.ts:125), so the cancellation chain is real. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/workflow-review-rpc.ts, src/daemon/code-review-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The in-daemon review client keeps reviewStreamRequest's failure behaviour 'exactly', with an aborted signal failing as ReviewStreamError('closed').","evidence":"daemon-stream.ts:455: `function onAbort(): void { failWith('aborted', `${method}: aborted by client`); }`. Today an abort gives failure 'aborted', not 'closed'; 'closed' is the socket-close case (:528). The callers key retryability and the error code off this value: start.ts:142 `RETRYABLE = new Set(['unreachable','closed','timeout'])` and start.ts:172 `code: `daemon-review-${failure}``, with the same pattern at handler.ts:669/723. Mapping an abort to 'closed' changes the code and makes it retryable. [files: src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts, src/mcp/review-step/phases/start.ts, src/mcp/code-review-step/handler.ts]","action":"Map an aborted signal to ReviewStreamError('aborted') in the in-daemon client, as today, or state the change on purpose and update the equivalence test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The four multi-turn state stores have 100-entry LRU and 1 h TTL limits and a 'server restarted' miss message, and they move unchanged.","evidence":"MAX_ENTRIES = 100 and TTL_MS = 60*60*1_000 appear in analyze-step, workflow-step, review-step and code-review-step state-store.ts. Each miss message contains 'not found: server restarted, TTL expired' (e.g. workflow-step/state-store.ts:56). [files: src/mcp/analyze-step/state-store.ts, src/mcp/workflow-step/state-store.ts, src/mcp/review-step/state-store.ts, src/mcp/code-review-step/state-store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"getLanceConn has no owner check today; setLanceConnPath exists for tests; the owner declaration to reuse is declareLiveStoreOwner, called by the daemon entry; DaemonUnreachableError and DaemonTooOldError are new.","evidence":"conn.ts:56-80 runs mkdirSync and lancedb.connect with no check, and conn.ts:42 has setLanceConnPath. lancedb.connect appears only in conn.ts. daemon/index.ts:117 calls declareLiveStoreOwner(). No class DaemonUnreachableError or DaemonTooOldError exists under src (ipc-client.ts only classifies ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED at :77). No worker_threads in the daemon would be refused by the new rule. [files: src/db/lance/conn.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The list of importers outside src/mcp that must be repointed to src/daemon/steps is complete.","evidence":"A grep for imports of analyze-step, workflow-step, build-step, review-step, code-review-step, triage-step, bundle-md, sampling-bridge and progress-forward outside src/mcp found exactly the files the LLD lists: workflow-rpc.ts:46, analyze-rpc-measure.test.ts:37-38 (bundle-md and oneShotRunParams from mcp/server.js), answer-step-failed-callers.test.ts, report-head.test.ts, executor-lmdb.test.ts, completeness.live.test.ts, lookup-measure.test.ts, the three code-review conditional tests, and mcp-sampling-provider.test.ts.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The handlers' reads of the MCP process's cwd and INSRC_REPO are confined to resolveRepoPath, the code-review fallback at handler.ts:256 and the one-shot analyze, so the StepCallContext covers them.","evidence":"In src/mcp, all handler reads go through resolveRepoPath (workflow-step start/resolve-question/review-deferred, triage start, build implement/validate, review start, analyze start) or through handler.ts:256. But code the moved analyze path reaches also reads the process's cwd: src/analyze/context/scope.ts:180 `return dir === '' || dir === '.' ? process.cwd() : dir;` (directoryOf, for a bare file name). Inside the daemon this resolves against the daemon's cwd, not the caller's. [files: src/analyze/context/scope.ts]","action":"Add scope.ts directoryOf to the context's readers (read StepCallContext.cwd when inside a step.call), or state that a bare relative file scope is resolved against the daemon's cwd.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The in-daemon client 'calls the registry's handler functions in-process' (workflow.review, codeReview.run/grounding/freshness, repo.resolveForCwd).","evidence":"No accessible registry exists to call. The handler maps are object literals built inline in src/daemon/index.ts ('repo.resolveForCwd' :615, 'codeReview.grounding' :752, 'codeReview.freshness' :772, 'codeReview.run' :1877, 'workflow.review' :1884) and held privately by the server (server.ts:81 `private readonly streamHandlers`). Nothing exports them. The LLD names no change site for how the step host gets them (for example, passing the maps into the step host at construction in index.ts). [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Name the wiring: build the in-daemon client in daemon/index.ts from the same handler maps passed to the server (or extract those handlers into importable modules), and list index.ts as a call site.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Deleting the reader allowance touches store.ts (_mayReadLiveStore, declareLiveStoreReaderUntilS11), its one call in server.ts:1258, the store-child 'declare-reader' command and the reader cases of the two tests.","evidence":"grep finds store.ts:320/333-335/365/372, server.ts:1258, store-child.ts:81/259-260, live-store-refusal.test.ts:63 and live-store-owner.test.ts:32/138/149. The LLD covers all of them. Also in store.ts but not named: assertMayOpen (:365) and resetLiveStoreDeclarationsForTests (:372) reference _mayReadLiveStore. Both are in the file being edited and the compiler will flag them. Note that the existing scan (live-store-owner.test.ts:154) skips __tests__.","action":"Optional: mention assertMayOpen and resetLiveStoreDeclarationsForTests in §2.7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored data changes. Mixed versions are handled: a new MCP server against an old daemon gets DaemonTooOldError from the 'unknown method' answer, and an old MCP server keeps its allowance until its session restarts.","evidence":"The step stores are in-memory Maps (state-store.ts), so moving them rewrites no data. The old daemon answers an unknown stream method with a plain 'unknown method:' line (server.ts:215), which the forwarder detects as reviewStreamRequest does today (daemon-stream.ts:489). The allowance is a module variable (store.ts:320), so the LLD is right that deleting it from the source does not reach a running old MCP process. Step 6 handles this with an lsof check. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/db/graph/store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design does not redesign anything owned by s4 or another Story: it only deletes the allowance s4 marked as removed by s11, and reuses s4's owner declaration.","evidence":"The store.ts:327-331 comment says 'Story s11 … DELETES this function and its one call (src/mcp/server.ts) — criterion ac6 of that Story'. The LLD reuses declareLiveStoreOwner and LmdbStoreNotOwnerError (store.ts:168) unchanged. Extending the owner rule to Lance is a new rule rather than a redesign of s4's, and the LLD flags it in §9. [files: src/db/graph/store.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A handler that throws inside the daemon is detectable and produces an error frame the forwarder can turn into an isError envelope.","evidence":"Even without the step host's own catch, server.ts:242-246 already sends `{ stream: 'error', data: { error: msg, recoverable: true } }` when a stream handler throws and the signal is not aborted. The LLD's step-host catch with code 'step-failed' is detectable on top of that. Note the existing error frame's data has no `code` field, so the forwarder must look for the step host's own frame to tell 'step-unknown-tool' from a generic failure. [files: src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac6 maps to at least one concrete test, including cancellation and the source scan that replaces 'exactly two places'.","evidence":"The §5 acceptance table maps ac1-ac6 to named unit, integration and smoke tests. The existing scan at live-store-owner.test.ts:147 ('appears at exactly two places') is replaced by an any-occurrence scan that builds the name at run time, and the reader case of live-store-refusal.test.ts:63 is turned into a refusal case. Cancellation is tested by observing the inner run's abort. [files: src/db/graph/__tests__/live-store-owner.test.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/live-store-refusal.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T11:14:25.200Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
